   "id": "kiddushin.57b.6",
   "daf": "57b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "בִּשְׂעַר נָזִיר. מְנָלַן? דְּאָמַר קְרָא ״קָדֹשׁ יִהְיֶה גַּדֵּל פֶּרַע שְׂעַר רֹאשׁוֹ״ – גִּידּוּלוֹ יִהְיֶה קָדוֹשׁ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that if a man betroths a woman «with a nazirite’s hair,» she is not betrothed. The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive that one is prohibited from deriving benefit from a nazirite’s hair? The Gemara answers: «As the verse states» with regard to a nazirite: «“He shall be holy [kadosh], he shall let the locks of the hair of his head grow long”» (Numbers 6:5), which teaches: «His» hair «growth shall be holy.»"
  }
